def dfs(graph, v, visited, order):
    visited.add(v)
    order.append(v)
    for n in sorted(graph[v]):
        if n not in visited:
            dfs(graph, n, visited, order)
    return order

print(dfs(graph, 'A', set(), []))  # ['A', 'B', 'D', 'C', 'E']
Go to the first unvisited neighbour and keep going; back up only when stuck. sorted() makes the order predictable, since sets have none.

