from itertools import combinations
nums = [3, 9, 8, 4]
target = 12
for r in range(len(nums) + 1):
    for combo in combinations(nums, r):
        if sum(combo) == target:
            print(combo)
# (3, 9)
# (8, 4)
Subset sum: does some group of numbers add up to the target? Trying every group works, but there are 2**n groups.

def check(nums, chosen, target):
    for x in chosen:
        if x not in nums:
            return False
    return sum(chosen) == target

print(check([3, 9, 8, 4], [8, 4], 12))  # True
print(check([3, 9, 8, 4], [3, 8], 12))  # False
Verifying takes about n steps even though finding took 2**n. NP is the class of problems whose proposed answers can be checked in polynomial time; every problem in P is also in NP.
